int Swings", "summary": "The 12k won by resignation, though Opus 5.5 held the lead for most of the game. By turn 19 the analysis had Opus 5.5 ahead by 22.1 points, helped by the 12k's own blunders at H3 and D1. Then J4 on turn 22 gave back 21.4 points, and D5 on turn 30 lost another 20.6, putting Black ahead by 23.5. Opus 5.5 resigned at turn 46 with Black ahead by 18.4.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "The 12k's H3 lost 10.0 points, taking Black's lead from -4.7 to -14.6 against the engine's choice of F4. This was the first big gift of the game, and it left Opus 5.5 comfortably ahead."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "The 12k's D1 lost 12.1 points, moving the lead from -4.4 to -16.5, while the engine preferred F6. It came right after Opus 5.5's D2, which had itself lost 7.5 points, and it more than undid that damage."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "This was the turning point. White stood at -21.8 on the board, with stones along the third and fourth lines and Black's stones on the second line squeezed beneath them. J4 lost 21.4 points and put the lead at -0.4, so the game was level again. The engine wanted E7."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "Black had reached +2.9, and D5 lost 20.6 points, swinging it to +23.5. The engine's choice was F4, which Black then took on turn 31, leaving the lead unchanged at +23.5. This was the second twenty-point loss, and Opus 5.5 never got back from it."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "H8 lost 7.9 points and pushed the lead up to +26.4. The 12k's H7 lost 7.9 straight back, to +18.4. Opus 5.5 resigned two moves later, still trailing by 18.4."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py (run on pasted boards in commands 2 and 3) only flood-fills the groups on the current position and prints each group's stones and liberties; it never tries or ranks moves or looks ahead. The other commands (cat, tail, grep, sed, and appends/edits to games.md and CLAUDE.md) just read and write notes.", "stop": false}}